The low-level GC on the linear-memory wasm target never traced object monitors (the C target got the same fix
upstream in f30b56fea, after this backend was removed). There a monitor lives in the object header's second word,
encoded (address >>> 1) | 0x80000000 (WasmGenerationVisitor.storeMonitor), and the GC's reference-field layouts
exclude it, so a Monitor reachable only from a header was collected while in use; the next synchronized on that
object wrote into freed memory, and the collector later walked a corrupted region forever (mctick: an endless
GC.markFromRegion during block bootstrap). Now, on this target only (PlatformDetector.isWebAssembly):
  - marking an object marks its header monitor; so does marking from classes (class objects live outside the heap,
    and synchronized (X.class) gives them monitors too);
  - updating pointers re-encodes the header word after the Monitor moves (from the relocation backup when the
    object itself moves, as upstream's C fix does).
String literals used as locks are not covered (outside the heap and not enumerated here).
Codegen: the GC's own code on this target; nothing in user code.

